  ],
  "text": "This storm was already old when your great great grandparents were born. Every storm you have ever sat through was gone within a week. Storms die here because they drag across land, hills, coastlines, rooftops. But Jupiter has no land at all, not one square metre of ground. So nothing ever slows the spin, and the storm just keeps turning. That single storm is wider than our entire planet. Winds inside it run at over four hundred kilometres an hour. But here is the strange part. It is getting smaller every year. A hundred and forty years ago it was more than twice as wide. You might be alive when a three hundred year old storm finally stops. One of these every day. Follow so you do not miss tomorrow.",
  "voice": "802e3bc2b27e49c2995d23ef70e6ac89",
  "model": "s2.1-pro"
}
